    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44669" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔπαις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παιδος</span>,
			ὁ, ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>blest with children</i>, i.e.
				<i>with many</i> or <i>with good, fine children,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				h.Hom.
				30.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.32
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hec.</u>
				810
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀσκληπιός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Pl.</u>
					639
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βιοτά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ion</u>
					491
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀθῆναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					6.330
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
			</span></i>); but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λατοῦς γόνος
			εὔπαις</span> her <i>noble son</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>HF</u>
				689
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IT</u>
				1234
			</span></i> (both lyr.).</div>
